    seeing:
      "The Danubian Plain is a broad east–west band of lowland across northern Bulgaria, bordered by the Danube to the north and the Fore-Balkan hills at the northern foot of the Balkan Mountains to the south. The Vit and Yantra rivers divide it into western, central and eastern sections, and Pleven is the main city in its central part. The terrain undulates gently, and it is one of Bulgaria's important grain-growing regions.",
