      "The Danubian Plain rests on the stable Moesian Platform, whose rock layers are nearly horizontal. In the Pleistocene, wind carried great quantities of dust from dry, cold regions and piled it on the platform as thick loess and loess-like deposits. Rivers flowing north from the Balkan Mountains later cut valley after valley into the loess tableland, and where limestone is exposed, water dissolved gorges and karst landforms.",
